                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2fd6f721-e61c-3c66-a24d-4d4ecd9587b5",
                                        "entry_id": "451ec183-1fe0-3d38-989f-87ed7f63a897",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A notional column of water from the surface to the bottom in a natural setting, notable for the differences in physical and chemical properties at various depths."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6fd0cd60-47ec-3622-963b-1468ff5eb913",
                                        "entry_id": "451ec183-1fe0-3d38-989f-87ed7f63a897",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The zone in which ascent and descent occur."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b7eb30fc-0940-393c-9ae7-fbceb158ddbd",
                                        "entry_id": "451ec183-1fe0-3d38-989f-87ed7f63a897",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A column alongside a railway track used to replenish a steam engine's water supply."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "29370b3e-1250-4aef-ba04-ebbfd722fadc",
                                                "sense_id": "b7eb30fc-0940-393c-9ae7-fbceb158ddbd",
                                                "text": "At Carlisle, as is customary, there was a very slow stop for the engine to draw to the water column."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "110cd2d6-d747-4885-ac86-b524d588a6c0",
                                                "sense_id": "b7eb30fc-0940-393c-9ae7-fbceb158ddbd",
                                                "text": "There could be no easy reversion to the pre-electrification timetable, as that provided for working over the Hyndland branch, which no longer existed, and new stations had come into use at Hyndland and Garscadden; moreover, water columns all along the routes concerned had been removed."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5b14bfba-5e59-4ccd-aad6-318a3e9bce02",
                                                "sense_id": "b7eb30fc-0940-393c-9ae7-fbceb158ddbd",
                                                "text": "Recent acquisitions include LMS open No 7991, formerly on the Severn Valley Railway, several wagons and a swan-necked water column."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d85b740c-0812-3752-8998-30c7fc38ddc9",
                                        "entry_id": "451ec183-1fe0-3d38-989f-87ed7f63a897",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The column of water inside the graduated cylinder of a pressure gauge that measures pressure in inches of water."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
